{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q413894","formula":"C₁₄H₁₆N₂","hill":"C14H16N2","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"H":16.0,"N":2.0},"names":{"en":"Atipamezole"},"descriptions":{"en":"Atipamezole, sold under the brand name Antisedan among others, is a synthetic α2 adrenergic receptor antagonist used for the reversal of the sedative and analgesic effects of dexmedetomidine and medetomidine in dogs. Its reversal effect works by competing with the sedative for α2-adrenergic receptors and displacing them. It is mainly used in veterinary medicine, and while it is only licensed for dogs and for intramuscular use, it has been used intravenously, as well as in cats and other animals (intravenous use in cats and dogs is not recommended due to the potential for cardiovascular collapse."},"fame":9,"pubchemCid":71310,"mass":212.29,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCC1(CC2=CC=CC=C2C1)C3=CN=CN3","inchikey":"HSWPZIDYAHLZDD-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"5-(2-ethyl-1,3-dihydroinden-2-yl)-1H-imidazole","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"71310","atoms":32,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.413,"y":0.78,"z":-0.954,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.654,"y":2.078,"z":0.832,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.66,"y":-0.944,"z":-0.266,"el":"C"},{"x":0.297,"y":-0.648,"z":-1.469,"el":"C"},{"x":0.313,"y":-1.293,"z":0.909,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.53,"y":-2.186,"z":-0.548,"el":"C"},{"x":1.518,"y":-0.119,"z":-0.779,"el":"C"},{"x":1.526,"y":-0.481,"z":0.571,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.568,"y":0.295,"z":-0.009,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.459,"y":-2.474,"z":0.611,"el":"C"},{"x":2.565,"y":0.6,"z":-1.331,"el":"C"},{"x":2.58,"y":-0.134,"z":1.399,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.725,"y":1.099,"z":1.082,"el":"C"},{"x":3.626,"y":0.966,"z":-0.501,"el":"C"},{"x":3.634,"y":0.602,"z":0.855,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.049,"y":1.858,"z":-0.402,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.107,"y":0.079,"z":-2.181,"e